<h2 id="s6"><span>06</span>Orders and access to the service</h2>
<p><strong>6.1.</strong> An order is placed by completing the checkout steps and pressing the button that explicitly indicates the obligation to pay (“Checkout”), as required by Art. 8 of GEO 34/2014. The order is an offer to purchase addressed to the Seller.</p>
<p><strong>6.2.</strong> After placing it, the Customer automatically receives an e-mail acknowledging the order, in accordance with Law no. 365/2002 on electronic commerce. That e-mail confirms receipt of the order, not its acceptance.</p>
<p><strong>6.3.</strong> The contract is concluded when the Seller sends the dispatch confirmation, or, for card payments, when the payment is confirmed.</p>
<p><strong>6.4.</strong> The Seller may refuse or cancel an order, informing the Customer, where:</p>
