<p><strong>6.5.</strong> If a Product becomes unavailable after the order is placed, the Customer is informed as soon as possible and may choose a replacement, a postponement or cancellation of the order with a full refund.</p>

<h2 id="s7"><span>07</span>Products, prices, payment and delivery</h2>
<p><strong>7.1. Prices.</strong> All prices are in Romanian lei (RON) and include VAT and the excise duty applicable to alcoholic beverages under the Romanian Fiscal Code. Prices do not include delivery, which is shown separately before the order is completed (Art. 6 of GEO 34/2014). The price displayed when the order is placed applies.</p>
<p><strong>7.2.</strong> Where a price reduction is announced, we indicate the prior price, i.e. the lowest price applied in the 30 days before the reduction, in accordance with GO 21/1992 as amended by GO 58/2022.</p>
<p><strong>7.3. Payment.</strong> Payment is made by the methods shown at checkout: <strong>bank card</strong>, processed securely by our partner payment processor (the Seller does not store card data), or <strong>cash on delivery</strong>, where available. No additional fee is charged for card payments.</p>
<p><strong>7.4. Invoicing.</strong> The invoice is issued on the basis of the details provided by the Customer, who is responsible for their accuracy. It is sent electronically to the e-mail address provided and, where required by law, transmitted through the Romanian RO e-Factura system (Law no. 296/2023, GEO 120/2021). By accepting the Terms, the Customer agrees to receive the invoice electronically.</p>
<p><strong>7.5. Delivery.</strong> Delivery is made by courier, within Romania only, to the address given in the order. The estimated time and costs are shown on the <a href="{{ pages['livrare-si-plata'].url }}">Delivery and payment</a> page; unless otherwise agreed, the Products are delivered within 30 days of the conclusion of the contract (Art. 18 of GEO 34/2014). The risk of loss or damage passes to the Customer on taking physical possession of the Products (Art. 20).</p>
<p><strong>7.6.</strong> We recommend checking the parcel on receipt, in the presence of the courier. Visible damage should be recorded in the courier's report and reported to the Seller as soon as possible. The Products are excise goods delivered in sealed packaging with the fiscal marking applied by the producer.</p>

<h2 id="s8"><span>08</span>Consumer rights and liability</h2>
<div class="zk-legal__callout">
  <strong>8.1. Right of withdrawal — 14 days.</strong>
  <p>As a consumer you may withdraw from the contract without giving any reason within 14 calendar days from the day on which you, or a third party designated by you other than the carrier, take physical possession of the Products (Art. 9 of GEO 34/2014), by an unequivocal statement sent to <a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a> or via the form on the <a href="{{ pages['politica-de-retur'].url }}">Returns policy</a> page.</p>
</div>
<p><strong>8.2.</strong> The Products must be returned without undue delay and no later than 14 days from the day you communicate your withdrawal; the direct cost of returning them is borne by the Customer (Art. 14). The Seller refunds all amounts received, including the cost of standard delivery, no later than 14 days from being informed, and may withhold the refund until the Products, or proof of their dispatch, are received (Art. 13). The Customer is liable for any diminished value resulting from handling beyond what is necessary to establish the nature and characteristics of the Products.</p>
<p><strong>8.3. Exception</strong> (Art. 16(e) of GEO 34/2014): the right of withdrawal does not apply to sealed Products which have been unsealed after delivery and cannot be returned for health protection or hygiene reasons. Bottles whose seal, capsule or tax strip has been opened or damaged cannot be returned, unless the Product is non-conforming.</p>
<p><strong>8.4. Conformity.</strong> The Seller is liable for any lack of conformity existing at delivery, under GEO 140/2021, for 2 years. In the event of a lack of conformity you are entitled, in the order set by law, to have the Product brought into conformity (replacement), to a proportionate price reduction or to termination of the contract, free of charge. The natural sediment of fruit distillates, natural colour variation between batches and damage caused by improper storage after delivery do not constitute a lack of conformity.</p>
<p><strong>8.5. Complaints.</strong> Complaints may be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a>{% if phone != blank %} or {{ phone }}{% endif %}; we reply within 30 calendar days.</p>
<p><strong>8.6. Liability.</strong> The Seller is liable to the consumer as provided by law. The Seller is not liable for irresponsible consumption of the Products or consumption contrary to legal requirements, for non-performance due to force majeure (unforeseeable and insurmountable events, including courier or payment service outages beyond the Seller's control), or for the content of third-party sites the Site may link to. Nothing in these Terms limits the rights granted to consumers by mandatory law.</p>

